Link LLVMObjCARCOpts among the LLVM components

pocl_llvm_build.cc pulls in llvm::createObjCARCContractPass() through clang's
backend headers, but LLVMObjCARCOpts is missing from the component list. It
goes unnoticed wherever LLVM is built as a single libLLVM dylib, since pocl
then links that one library and gets every symbol; the mingw target builds LLVM
with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS, so pocl links the components listed here and the link
fails on that symbol.

diff --git a/cmake/SetupLLVMviaCMake.cmake b/cmake/SetupLLVMviaCMake.cmake
--- a/cmake/SetupLLVMviaCMake.cmake
+++ b/cmake/SetupLLVMviaCMake.cmake
@@ -146,6 +146,7 @@ set(POCL_LLVM_COMPONENTS
   LLVMExecutionEngine
   LLVMTarget
   LLVMPasses
+  LLVMObjCARCOpts
   LLVMTargetParser
   LLVMLibDriver
   LLVMWindowsDriver
